  "METHODOLOGY_CORRECTION_2026-07-12": {
    "rule": "NEVER pool |move|. Bucket every release by signed SURPRISE x signed REACTION; report per-bucket SIGNED stats + directional hit-rate. Pooled |move| measures VOLATILITY/repricing, NOT directional edge.",
    "surprise_proxy": "ENERGY: actual weekly EIA change - 5yr same-ISO-week avg (SEASONAL proxy for street consensus; captures seasonal surprise, not exact desk number). MACRO: NFP vs trailing-12mo trend (WEAK phase-2 proxy). Real consensus-conditioned version comes FORWARD via ForexFactory polling.",
    "reframe": "Directional tradeable content is INVERTED from the |move| volatility ranking: natgas=biggest mover but seasonal-surprise sign is a COIN FLIP; crude=modest mover but ~60% directional hit-rate on the release DAY.",
    "natgas_regime_correction": "Regimes are DATA-DISCOVERED (not calendar): double-humped demand \u2014 winter-withdrawal(HDD>120), summer-withdrawal(CDD>40, a build-MINIMUM on the national aggregate not a net draw), spring/fall injection. Withdrawal humps are the biggest MOVERS but the seasonal proxy is directionally BLINDEST in winter because weather owns the number (LINK A R2=0.85). Weather chain: weather->storage STRONG, storage->price-at-release ~0."
  },
